  "objective": "Measure four silence-handling variants of this network's best AMM file before submitting it to Paradigm's AMM fee challenge (paradigm.xyz/puzzles/amm). BS = stack-b (seat 827) + silence-a (seat 534) from goal 052122ee: +0.736 se 0.018 over NP2 on 2,000 fresh seeds. silence-b (seat 494) used the same silence mechanism with stronger settings and scored +0.410 alone versus silence-a's +0.219, so each VAR swaps BS's silence settings (cap on silent steps, per-step keep factor, damping) toward silence-b's. Each block runs NP2, BS and one VAR separately against the 30 bps Vanilla on the same 2,000 fresh seeds. Simulator: github.com/benedictbrady/amm-challenge @ 6b6921f8d463314aa7c96234e1be25a25245f704.",
